      <li><a href="#clause-8">8. Keeping your information safe</a></li>
      <li><a href="#clause-9">9. Clients' personal data</a></li>
      <li><a href="#clause-10">10. Changes to this policy</a></li>
    </ol>
  </nav>
  <section class="legal-section" id="clause-1">
    <h2 class="legal-heading">1. Information we collect</h2>
    <div class="legal-clause"><span class="legal-num">1.1</span><div class="legal-text">
      <p><strong>When you contact us.</strong> If you use the enquiry form on our website or email us, we collect your first and last name, email address, company name and the content of your message.</p>
    </div></div>
    <div class="legal-clause"><span class="legal-num">1.2</span><div class="legal-text">
      <p><strong>When you visit our website.</strong> We and our service providers collect technical information such as your IP address, browser and device type, the pages you visit and how you arrived at our site. Some of this is collected using cookies (see <a href="#cookies">section 5</a>).</p>
    </div></div>
    <div class="legal-clause"><span class="legal-num">1.3</span><div class="legal-text">
      <p><strong>When we work with you or your organisation.</strong> We collect the business contact details of the people we deal with at our clients, suppliers and partners, such as names, job titles, work email addresses and phone numbers, and records of our correspondence and meetings.</p>
    </div></div>
    <div class="legal-clause"><span class="legal-num">1.4</span><div class="legal-text">
      <p><strong>When you appear in our work or on our website.</strong> If you take part in a film, interview, event or other project, or we feature you on our website (for example in our KOL Hub, a case study or a testimonial), we hold your name, professional role and organisation, and images, video and audio recordings of you.</p>
    </div></div>
  </section>
  <section class="legal-section" id="clause-2">
    <h2 class="legal-heading">2. How we use your information and why</h2>
    <div class="legal-clause"><span class="legal-num">2.1</span><div class="legal-text">
      <p>Data protection law requires us to have a lawful basis for each way we use personal information. We use it:</p>
      <ol class="legal-list">
        <li><span class="legal-num">(a)</span><p>to reply to your enquiry and discuss working together. Our lawful basis is our legitimate interest in responding to people who contact us and developing our business;</p></li>
        <li><span class="legal-num">(b)</span><p>to provide our services and manage our relationships with clients, suppliers and partners, including sending and paying invoices. Our lawful bases are the performance of our contract with you or your organisation and our legitimate interest in running our business;</p></li>
        <li><span class="legal-num">(c)</span><p>to produce and promote our work, including showing the people who appear in it on our website and in our portfolio. Our lawful basis is our legitimate interest in producing and promoting our work, or your consent where we have asked for it, for example in a contributor release form;</p></li>
        <li><span class="legal-num">(d)</span><p>to understand how our website is used and to improve it. Our lawful basis is our legitimate interest in running an effective website, and your consent where the law requires it for cookies;</p></li>
        <li><span class="legal-num">(e)</span><p>to keep our website and systems secure. Our lawful basis is our legitimate interest in protecting our business; and</p></li>
        <li><span class="legal-num">(f)</span><p>to meet our legal, tax and accounting obligations and to establish, exercise or defend legal claims. Our lawful bases are compliance with a legal obligation and our legitimate interests.</p></li>
      </ol>
    </div></div>
    <div class="legal-clause"><span class="legal-num">2.2</span><div class="legal-text">
      <p>We may send people we work with, or who have contacted us, occasional emails about our work that we think are relevant to them in a business context. You can ask us to stop at any time by replying to one of those emails or contacting us.</p>
    </div></div>
    <div class="legal-clause"><span class="legal-num">2.3</span><div class="legal-text">
      <p>We do not sell your personal information, and we do not use it to make decisions about you by automated means.</p>
    </div></div>
  </section>
  <section class="legal-section" id="clause-3">
    <h2 class="legal-heading">3. Who we share it with</h2>
    <div class="legal-clause"><span class="legal-num">3.1</span><div class="legal-text">
      <p>We share personal information only where we need to, with:</p>
      <ol class="legal-list">
        <li><span class="legal-num">(a)</span><p>service providers who help us run our business and website, such as our website host (Netlify, which also receives enquiry form submissions), analytics provider (Google Analytics), video host (Vimeo), email (Microsoft 365), file storage and transfer (Dropbox), video review (Replay) and accounting providers. They may only use it to provide their services to us;</p></li>
        <li><span class="legal-num">(b)</span><p>freelancers and subcontractors who work with us on a project;</p></li>
        <li><span class="legal-num">(c)</span><p>our professional advisers, such as accountants, lawyers and insurers; and</p></li>
        <li><span class="legal-num">(d)</span><p>the police, regulators, courts or other authorities, where the law requires it or it is needed to protect our rights.</p></li>
      </ol>
    </div></div>
    <div class="legal-clause"><span class="legal-num">3.2</span><div class="legal-text">
      <p>If we sell or restructure our business, personal information may be passed to the new owner, who may use it in the ways described in this policy.</p>
    </div></div>
  </section>
  <section class="legal-section" id="clause-4">
    <h2 class="legal-heading">4. International transfers</h2>
    <div class="legal-clause"><span class="legal-num">4.1</span><div class="legal-text">
      <p>Some of our service providers are based in, or store information in, countries outside the UK, including the United States. Where we transfer personal information outside the UK, we make sure it is protected, for example by relying on UK adequacy regulations (including the UK Extension to the EU-US Data Privacy Framework) or by using the UK's approved international data transfer agreement or addendum.</p>
    </div></div>
  </section>
  <section class="legal-section" id="cookies">
    <h2 class="legal-heading">5. Cookies</h2>
    <div class="legal-clause"><span class="legal-num">5.1</span><div class="legal-text">
      <p>Cookies are small files stored on your device when you visit a website. Our website uses:</p>
      <ol class="legal-list">
        <li><span class="legal-num">(a)</span><p><strong>strictly necessary cookies</strong>, which the website needs to work properly; and</p></li>
        <li><span class="legal-num">(b)</span><p><strong>analytics cookies</strong> set by Google Analytics, which tell us how many people visit our website, which pages they look at and how they found us. Google Analytics uses identifiers such as your IP address and a unique device ID.</p></li>
      </ol>
    </div></div>
    <div class="legal-clause"><span class="legal-num">5.2</span><div class="legal-text">
      <p>When you play a video on our website, Vimeo may also set cookies. These are covered by <a href="https://vimeo.com/cookie_policy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Vimeo's cookie policy</a>.</p>
    </div></div>
    <div class="legal-clause"><span class="legal-num">5.3</span><div class="legal-text">
      <p>You can block or delete cookies in your browser settings, and you can stop Google Analytics collecting information about you with <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google's opt-out browser add-on</a>. Blocking strictly necessary cookies may stop parts of the website working.</p>
    </div></div>
  </section>
  <section class="legal-section" id="clause-6">
    <h2 class="legal-heading">6. How long we keep it</h2>
    <div class="legal-clause"><span class="legal-num">6.1</span><div class="legal-text">
      <p>We keep personal information only for as long as we need it:</p>
      <ol class="legal-list">
        <li><span class="legal-num">(a)</span><p>enquiries that do not lead to work: up to 2 years after our last contact;</p></li>
        <li><span class="legal-num">(b)</span><p>client, supplier and contract records, including invoices: 6 years after the end of the relevant financial year or contract, to meet tax and legal requirements;</p></li>
        <li><span class="legal-num">(c)</span><p>website analytics information: up to 14 months; and</p></li>
        <li><span class="legal-num">(d)</span><p>recordings and images in our published work: for as long as the work is in use, or as agreed with you.</p></li>
      </ol>
    </div></div>
    <div class="legal-clause"><span class="legal-num">6.2</span><div class="legal-text">
      <p>After that, we securely delete or anonymise it.</p>
    </div></div>
  </section>
  <section class="legal-section" id="clause-7">
    <h2 class="legal-heading">7. Your rights</h2>
    <div class="legal-clause"><span class="legal-num">7.1</span><div class="legal-text">
      <p>You have the right to:</p>
      <ol class="legal-list">
        <li><span class="legal-num">(a)</span><p>ask for a copy of the personal information we hold about you;</p></li>
        <li><span class="legal-num">(b)</span><p>ask us to correct information that is wrong or incomplete;</p></li>
        <li><span class="legal-num">(c)</span><p>ask us to delete your information;</p></li>
        <li><span class="legal-num">(d)</span><p>ask us to restrict how we use your information;</p></li>
        <li><span class="legal-num">(e)</span><p>object to our use of your information where we rely on legitimate interests, and to stop direct marketing at any time;</p></li>
        <li><span class="legal-num">(f)</span><p>ask us to transfer information you gave us to another organisation, where we use it on the basis of consent or a contract; and</p></li>
        <li><span class="legal-num">(g)</span><p>withdraw your consent at any time, where we rely on consent. This does not affect anything we did before you withdrew it.</p></li>
      </ol>
    </div></div>
    <div class="legal-clause"><span class="legal-num">7.2</span><div class="legal-text">
      <p>Some of these rights apply only in certain circumstances. To use any of them, email <a href="mailto:hello@madeclearstudios.com">hello@madeclearstudios.com</a>. We will reply within one month.</p>
    </div></div>
    <div class="legal-clause"><span class="legal-num">7.3</span><div class="legal-text">
      <p>If you are unhappy with how we have handled your information, please tell us first so we can try to put it right. You also have the right to complain to the Information Commissioner's Office (ICO) at <a href="https://ico.org.uk/make-a-complaint/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">ico.org.uk</a> or on 0303 123 1113.</p>
    </div></div>
  </section>
  <section class="legal-section" id="clause-8">
    <h2 class="legal-heading">8. Keeping your information safe</h2>
    <div class="legal-clause"><span class="legal-num">8.1</span><div class="legal-text">
      <p>We use appropriate technical and organisational measures to protect personal information against loss, misuse and unauthorised access, and we only give access to people who need it.</p>
    </div></div>
  </section>
  <section class="legal-section" id="clause-9">
    <h2 class="legal-heading">9. Clients' personal data</h2>
    <div class="legal-clause"><span class="legal-num">9.1</span><div class="legal-text">
      <p>When we process personal data on behalf of a client as part of a project, we do so as the client's processor. The client's own privacy notice applies to that information, and our <a href="/terms-conditions#schedule-1">Terms and Conditions</a> set out how we handle it.</p>
    </div></div>
  </section>
  <section class="legal-section" id="clause-10">
    <h2 class="legal-heading">10. Changes to this policy</h2>
    <div class="legal-clause"><span class="legal-num">10.1</span><div class="legal-text">
      <p>We may update this policy from time to time. The latest version will always be on this page, with the date it was last updated.</p>
    </div></div>
  </section>
</div>
